# Income N Filing — Website Revamp Design Prompt

Design a complete website revamp for Income N Filing, a business tax and
compliance advisory firm based in Kolkata (second office in Bhagalpur),
serving clients since 2017, 500+ businesses served across ~94 services
in 10 categories (Incorporation, Government Registrations, Income Tax,
GST, Corporate Compliances, Insolvency Advices, Documentation Services,
Contracts, Accounting & Book Keeping, Ancillary Services). Positioning
line: "Simplifying Compliance. Empowering Business."

## Creative direction: Compliance OS

Reframe the brand from "tax firm with a website" to "compliance
software you talk to." The whole site should feel like operating a
dashboard, not scrolling a brochure. Two systems work together:

**1. Terminal search (hero, right side of homepage)**
A live-feeling command terminal — monospace type, blinking cursor,
placeholder text that cycles through example queries like
`> search gst registration`, `> search nri filing`, `> search trademark`.
As the user types, it filters the full service directory in real time,
autocomplete-style. Selecting a result "outputs" a response block like
a CLI return — service name, what it covers, turnaround expectation,
and a `[ book ]` command instead of a generic button. Break the
terminal module's palette on purpose — green-on-black or amber-on-black
against the rest of the site's navy/gold, like a system-within-a-system.
Every microcopy choice on the site should quietly inherit this
vocabulary: services are `available`, not "offered"; a completed
filing shows `status: deployed`; form submissions read like a command
executing.

**2. Dashboard logic (everything else)**
Stats aren't a static row of numbers — they read like a live ops
panel: status indicators, a subtle "next compliance deadline" ticker,
a pulse marker on the Bhagalpur/Kolkata office map. Service categories
on the Services Hub render as dashboard modules, not marketing cards.
The terminal search should feel like it's querying this dashboard, not
sitting decoratively in the hero disconnected from the rest of the
page.

Base palette: deep navy + gold/amber accent (carried over from current
brand), with the terminal module allowed to break into
green-on-black or amber-on-black as its own visual register.

## Required pages (14 — do not exceed)

1. **Home** — terminal hero, live-feeling stats/status bar, "How It
   Works" (3-step process), why-choose-us grid, testimonial preview,
   final CTA
2. **About** — mission/story, credibility stat grid, client logo strip
3. **Services Hub** — the full searchable directory; terminal search
   at full power here, 10 categories, ~94 services, routes into the 7
   flagship pages below or expands inline for the rest
4. **Live Chat** — a standalone page styled as a terminal-native chat
   interface (continues the `> ` command vocabulary from the hero:
   `> connect to advisor`, typed message appears as a command being
   issued). This is NOT a staffed live-chat backend — no ongoing
   agent infrastructure. On submit, the message routes straight to
   WhatsApp (primary, already positioned as "fastest response") with
   email as a visible fallback option. The page should feel like a
   live conversation with the compliance system itself, even though
   functionally it's a styled handoff to WhatsApp/email. No pricing,
   dollar figures, or numeric ranges anywhere on the site — payment
   and quote details are handled entirely through this direct contact
   channel, never published
5. **ITR Filing** (flagship service page)
6. **GST Registration & Filing** (flagship service page)
7. **Company Incorporation** (flagship service page)
8. **TCS Filing & Compliance** (flagship service page)
9. **Tax Notice Handling** (flagship service page)
10. **Capital Gains Advisory** (flagship service page)
11. **NRI Income Tax Filing** (flagship service page)
12. **Testimonials / Case Studies** — expand existing Google reviews
    into fuller case-study format
13. **FAQ** — standalone page, not a homepage section
14. **Contact** — traditional contact page: consultation form, phone/
    email/WhatsApp listed as channels, office locations (Bhagalpur +
    Kolkata), social links. Distinct from Live Chat — this is the
    formal "fill out a form" path, Live Chat is the conversational
    "talk now" path. Don't let the two collapse into duplicates of
    each other.

Nav: Home, About, Services (dropdown exposing the 7 flagship pages),
Live Chat, Testimonials, FAQ, Contact.

## Constraints

- Same color palette and typography system across all 14 pages, but
  each page needs its own layout logic — no repeated template
  stamped across pages. The 7 flagship service pages especially
  should differ from each other in structure (e.g. NRI Filing should
  read remote/international-user-aware; Company Incorporation should
  read more formal/B2B than ITR Filing).
- Original design system only — nothing that reads as a Webflow
  template or generic CA-firm site (avoid the beige-card,
  stock-photo-of-handshake look every competitor in this space uses).
- Brand tone: trustworthy and precise, not sterile-corporate. Client
  base spans first-time salaried ITR filers through startups and
  NRIs, so the design has to read credible to a novice and a
  business owner at once.
- Deliverable target: Next.js-compatible component structure — final
  code handoff will be built in Next.js.
